{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791702668,"nonce":"ijiiyjrouGENJHm43Unb6JvP4fE=","title":"An image with a border draws its square corners over a round border","message":"An img with a border and a border-radius was clipped to its node's outer rounded box but drawn in its content box, after the border: the photograph's square corners covered the border ring and were cut only at the outer edge. Seen in the wiki's avatars (a ring, a stack with white separations, a profile picture), each a square photo inside a white disc.\n\nCSS clips replaced content inside the border. The display list now clips an image or a canvas to its padding box, rounded by the radius left after a uniform border (the clip children of a clipping box already get); a borderless box keeps its own rounded box.\n\nFix: blinc_abi branch image-inner-clip, commit f1912c4 (worktree ../blinc_abi-image; native/Cargo.toml points at it locally, not committed). blinc_abi's lib tests pass. The display list is shared with the other SDK, so its maintaining agent is to be told before landing.\n\nTest: tests/native-image-element.mjs draws a solid red image in a round 8px white border and reads the ring at the diagonal; it fails against blinc_abi main and passes on the branch.\n\nThe wiki's avatars meanwhile use a round frame that clips its image, which was drawn correctly already.","files":null}]}